From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Greg Burd <greg@burd.me>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] zfs: force single-threaded inline ARC eviction on OSv

Parallel ARC eviction (zfs_arc_evict_threads > 1) dispatches arc_evict_task()
to the arc_evict taskq (AS0 worker threads).  When a forked PostgreSQL backend
triggers eviction under memory pressure it kmem_allocs the evict_arg_t array
and dispatches &eva[i] to those AS0 workers, then taskq_waits.  On OSv fork
model the worker running arc_evict_task races the dispatcher / touches state
whose VA is not coherent in the worker address space and faults on eva->eva_ml
(arc.c:4088, reached via handle_mmap_fault under the ZFS taskqueue).

Force zfs_arc_evict_threads = 1 in arc_evict_thread_init() so eviction runs
inline in the caller context via arc_evict_state_impl(), removing the taskq
hand-off and the race.  This is the same OSv serialization applied to libtpool
dispatch (patch 0021) and dataset mounting (patch 0022); parallel eviction is
a throughput optimization OSv does not require.

This patch touches only arc_evict_thread_init().  The ARC-sizing helper
arc_reduce_target_size_noshrink() and the small-RAM arc_c_min cap live in
patch 0009 (zfs: fix ARC sizing, memory pressure and OSv platform ...); they
are not repeated here.

Signed-off-by: Greg Burd <greg@burd.me>
---
 module/zfs/arc.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/module/zfs/arc.c b/module/zfs/arc.c
index 9912eb818..e0afb1f35 100644
--- a/module/zfs/arc.c
+++ b/module/zfs/arc.c
@@ -4096,6 +4096,24 @@ arc_evict_task(void *arg)
 static void
 arc_evict_thread_init(void)
 {
+#ifdef __OSV__
+	/*
+	 * Force single-threaded, inline ARC eviction on OSv.  Parallel eviction
+	 * dispatches arc_evict_task() to the arc_evict taskq (AS0 worker
+	 * threads).  When a forked PostgreSQL backend triggers eviction under
+	 * memory pressure it kmem_allocs the evict_arg_t array and dispatches
+	 * &eva[i] to those AS0 workers, then taskq_waits.  On OSv's fork model
+	 * the worker running arc_evict_task races the dispatcher's teardown /
+	 * touches state whose VA is not coherent in the worker's address space,
+	 * faulting on eva->eva_ml.  Inline eviction (zfs_arc_evict_threads == 1)
+	 * takes the direct arc_evict_state_impl() path in the caller's context,
+	 * removing the taskq hand-off and the race -- the same OSv serialization
+	 * applied to libtpool dispatch and dataset mounting (patches 0021/0022).
+	 * Parallel eviction is a throughput optimization OSv does not require.
+	 */
+	zfs_arc_evict_threads = 1;
+	return;
+#endif
 	if (zfs_arc_evict_threads == 0) {
 		/*
 		 * Compute number of threads we want to use for eviction.
